      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "could-not-extract: The draft lists the term with no definition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/smart-guidelines",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "SMART Guidelines"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "SMART guidelines",
        "SMART",
        "Standards-based, Machine-readable, Adaptive, Requirements-based, Testable Guidelines"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Standards-based, Machine-readable, Adaptive, Requirements-based, Testable Guidelines are a comprehensive set of reusable digital health components (e.g., interoperability standards, code libraries, algorithms, technical and operational specifications) that transform the guideline adaptation and implementation process to preserve fidelity and accelerate uptake. SMART Guidelines provide a five-step pathway to advance the adoption of best clinical and data practices, even if a country is not yet fully digital."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "SMART",
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own glossary wording, verbatim (folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md). Substantive and wording alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#139, smart-ra#140, smart-ra#142): (1) PHC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11) and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-011.md, p. 11): \"Standards-based, Machine-readable, Adaptive, Requirements-based, and Testable Guidelines are recommended digital capabilities, health and data content aligned with normative recommendations. They represent packages of comprehensive documentation and reusable digital health components (e.g. health content, interoperability standards, code libraries, algorithms, technical and operational specifications) that facilitate country adaptation and adoption of clinical and public health protocols, health systems strengthening recommendations, and data and interoperability standards into digital health information systems with fidelity. SMART Guidelines serve as a starting point and as foundational specifications to advance the development of robust person-centred digital systems. These specifications are software-agnostic, context-agnostic, and are applicable to all levels of digital maturity (10,23).\" (2) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"The WHO guidelines for developing Standards-based, Machine-readable, Adaptive, Requirements-based and Testable components for implementing digital health capabilities. The components include interoperability standards, code libraries, algorithms, and technical and operational specifications. The SMART Guidelines provide a five-step pathway to advance the adoption of best clinical and data practices, even if a country is not yet fully digital (12, 13).\" (3) PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"WHO standards-based, machine-readable, adaptive, requirements-based, and testable Guidelines are recommended digital capabilities, health and data content. They represent a comprehensive set of reusable digital health components (e.g., interoperability standards, code libraries, algorithms, technical and operational specifications) that transform the guideline adaptation and implementation process to preserve fidelity and accelerate uptake. SMART Guidelines provide a five-step pathway to advance the adoption of best clinical and data practices, even if a country is not yet fully digital.11, 12\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/snomed-ct",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "SNOMED CT"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "SNOMED",
        "CT",
        "SNOMED-CT",
        "Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine - Clinical Terms",
        "Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine – Clinical Terms"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms is a structured clinical terminology standard for use in electronic health records."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "SNOMED CT",
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own wording, verbatim. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/snomed-gps",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "SNOMED GPS"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "SNOMED-GPS",
        "Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine – Global Patient Set",
        "Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine-Global Patient Set",
        "GPS"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine – Global Patient Set is a list of basic clinical terms. It is an open and freely accessible subset of SNOMED CT terms that represents the breadth of concepts included in the SNOMED CT International Edition."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "SNOMED-GPS",
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own wording, verbatim. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review. Expanded in PHC handbook Abbreviations (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-001-abbreviations.md, p. 7) as \"SNOMED-GPS: Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine-Global Patient Set\" and cited in SFP handbook §4.4 (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-025-44-outline-data-requirements.md, page-042.md, p. 30).",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/solution-architecture",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Solution Architecture"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The design of a specific application component or HDPI expressed through specifications and diagrams"
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own wording, verbatim. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review. The draft marks this entry [Under review].",
      "skos:editorialNote": "Under review",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/stakeholder",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Stakeholder"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "stakeholder"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "An individual, role, or organisation with an interest in the outcomes of the architecture."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own glossary wording, verbatim (folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md). Substantive and wording alternatives across the corpus (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#140): (1) RA Table 3.1 (library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-026-31-the-architecture-description-approach.md): \"An individual, team, or organisation with interests in, or concerns relative to, the architecture.\" (2) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"In the context of digital health transformation, anyone who is affected by or interested in the consequences of the efforts, including the planning team, end users, beneficiaries and funders.\" (4) DIIG Annex 1.1 Glossary (who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-141.md, p. 129): \"Any person who is affected by or interested in the consequences of the digital health implementation; stakeholders include the planning team, end-users, beneficiaries and funders.\" (Also enumerated in SFP handbook §1.1, who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-009-11-analyse-key-stakeholders.md, page-020.md, p. 8.) All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/value",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Value"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The benefit or utility a stakeholder gains from using a service, product, or capability."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own wording, verbatim. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/actor-conformance-model",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Actor (Conformance Model)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "Actor",
        "actor (conformance model)"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "An Actor is an abstract, well-bounded role in the health information ecosystem that is defined entirely by the information-processing responsibilities it assumes and the interactions it participates in. An Actor is neither a software product nor an organisational unit."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "Defined in RA §3.7.2 (library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-050-372-the-model.md, p. 111–116). Substantive distinction from the platform's `actor` concept in folio-assistant-core/glossary/cat-harness.glossary.json (\"A concrete participant, human, agentic or mechanical, that persists across every process and takes on roles\"): the RA's conformance-model Actor is an abstract information-processing role realised by concrete systems, closer to IHE's Actor or the platform's Role (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "dcterms:source": "library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-050-372-the-model.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/adverse-events-following-immunization",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Adverse Events Following Immunization"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "AEFI",
        "Adverse effects following immunisation"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Adverse effects following immunisation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "AEFI",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Recorded per smart-ra#142 item 4: the PC handbook abbreviations list (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-006.md, p. 6) expands AEFI as \"Adverse effects following immunisation\", whereas standard WHO immunization terminology expands AEFI as \"Adverse events following immunization\" (an 'event' is any untoward medical occurrence following immunization and does not presuppose a causal 'effect'). Both expansions are recorded as candidates; neither is silently altered.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-006.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/business-process",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Business Process"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "business process"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A set of activities and tasks performed in coordination to achieve a specified business objective, or to deliver value in a specific way to a health service user. In the context of digitizing care pathways, this could include “health service user registration” and “referrals”, for example (see section 3.3)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8). Wording alternative in SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9, citing DIIG): \"A set of related activities or tasks performed together to achieve the objectives of the health programme area, such as registration, counselling and referrals (3).\" Both are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/data-dictionary",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Data Dictionary"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "data dictionary"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A singular storage location for information about the data elements, detailing their type and definition, relationships, origin and use."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8). Wording alternative in SFP handbook §4.4 body (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-025-44-outline-data-requirements.md, page-042.md, p. 30): \"A data dictionary is a repository of information about the data elements such as description, data type and other characteristics.\" Both are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, dth-sfp#1 P2).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/data-element"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/data-element",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Data Element"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "data element"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A unit of data that has a specific and precise meaning."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "Identical wording in PHC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8), PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8), and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9, citing ref. 4). Recorded as a shared candidate concept (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/deploy",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Deploy"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "deployment",
        "Deployment"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Make the software available for use beyond testing purposes."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording under 'Deploy' (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8). Wording alternative in SC handbook glossary under 'deployment' (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"Making a software system available for use beyond testing purposes.\" Both are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digital-transformation",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Digital Transformation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "digital transformation"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The process of digitally optimizing and driving systems-level changes by leveraging innovation, analytics and feedback mechanisms to improve person-centred health systems. Digital technologies are used to fundamentally change and improve how health services are delivered and accessed across all health programme areas (12,14,15)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8); identical wording (with minor punctuation/citation differences) in PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8) and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9). Wording alternative in SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8), which inverts the two sentences: \"In the health context, using digital technologies to fundamentally change and improve how health services are delivered and accessed across all health programme areas (3, 4, 5). The process involves using innovation, analytics and feedback mechanisms to achieve systems-level changes.\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digitization"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digitalization"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digitalization",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Digitalization"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "digitalization"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The process of digitally automating and simplifying processes to streamline individual health programmes and reduce manual efforts for greater efficiency (12,13)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8). Wording alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"In the health context, the process of digitally automating and simplifying processes to streamline individual health programmes and reduce manual efforts for greater efficiency. Digitalization is the second step in digital transformation (3, 6).\" (2) PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8) and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"The process of digitally automating and simplifying processes to streamline individual health programmes and reducing manual efforts for greater efficiency. Digitalization is the second step towards digital transformation.\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digitization"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digital-transformation"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digitization",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Digitization"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "digitization"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The process of converting and organizing data from paper records into a digital format for easier entry, storage and retrieval (12,16)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8). Wording alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"The process of converting and organizing data from manual paper records into a digital format for easier entry, storage and retrieval. Digitization is the initial step in digital transformation (3, 7).\" (2) PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8) and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"The process of converting and organizing data from paper records into a digital format for easier entry, storage and retrieval. Digitization is the initial step towards digital transformation.\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digitalization"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/digital-transformation"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/end-user",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "End-User"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "End user",
        "end user",
        "end users"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "People who will be using the digital system(s)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "Identical wording in PHC handbook glossary ('End-user', who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 8), PC handbook glossary ('End user', who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8), and SFP handbook glossary ('End user', who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9). Wording alternative in SC handbook glossary ('end users', who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"People who will be using the digital systems.\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/features",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Features"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "features"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The characteristics of a system that include look and feel as well as what the system can do (e.g. “reporting” can be a feature of a PCPOSS)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 9). Wording alternatives across the DTH corpus, differing only in domain example and 'a system' vs 'your system' (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"The characteristics of a system that include look and feel as well as what the system can do (e.g., “order processing” can be a feature of an order management solution).\" (2) PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8) and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"The characteristics of your system that include look and feel as well as what the system can do (e.g., “approval workflow” can be a feature of a product master data management solution).\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functions"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functional-requirements"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/full-stac",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Full-STAC"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "full-STAC",
        "Full Standards, Technologies, Architectures, and Content"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "An ecosystem specifying open standards, open technologies, open architectures, and open content (full-STAC)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Full-STAC",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Cites Mehl et al. 2023 (library/mehl-2023-full-stac-oqad018/, glossary/full-stac.glossary.json) in RA §2.2.2 (library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-022-222-the-enabling-conditions-for-reddhi.md). Linked via exactMatch to the full-STAC scheme (smart-ra#143).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/open-standards"
        },
