    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functional-requirements",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Functional Requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "functional requirements",
        "Functional requirements"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Description of what the digital system needs to do to support the tasks that make up the health system process and address the identified health system challenges (e.g. a PCPOSS must be able to remind health workers which health service users to follow-up with)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 9). Wording and substantive alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"A description of what the digital system needs to do to support the tasks that make up the business process and address the identified challenges.\" (2) PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"Description of what the digital system needs to do to support the tasks that make up the health system process and address the identified challenges (e.g., a product master data management solution must be able to define categories and attributes to organize product information).\" (3) SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"Capabilities the system must have to meet the end users’ needs and achieve tasks within the business process.\" All four are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/non-functional-requirements"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/features"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functions"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functions",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Functions"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "functions"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Functions in a system are how features are implemented (e.g. “calculating aggregate data” and “displaying feedback in the form of diagrams” are functions of the “reporting” feature of a PCPOSS)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 9). Substantive alternative in SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"Business processes within a system that help the system perform (e.g., “receiving inventory” and “picking inventory” are functions of the “warehousing” feature of a warehouse management system).\" (PHC defines functions as \"how features are implemented\"; SC defines them as \"Business processes within a system that help the system perform\".) Both are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/features"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functional-requirements"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/generic-product",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Generic Product"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "Generic product or product information",
        "product information",
        "generic national product code"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "In this handbook, the terms ‘generic product,’ ‘product,’ or ‘product information’ pertain to the general identifying details of a health product, excluding any manufacturer-specific information."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8), identical in SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-010.md, p. 10). Internal wording alternative in PC handbook Ch. 2 body (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-028.md, p. 28): \"Generic products can be described as generic items that conceal the brand or manufacturer information.\" Distinct from the RA's architectural `product` concept; both wordings are recorded as candidates and neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#139, smart-ra#142).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/trade-item"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/product-master-data"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/governance",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Governance"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "governance",
        "governance (health supply chain)"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Governance is the set of arrangements through which decision authority is distributed, exercised and accounted for across all those who depend upon, contribute to, or are served by the shared infrastructure."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "RA §3.4.1 body wording, verbatim (library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-029-341-purpose-and-framing.md, p. 64–65). Substantive alternative in SC handbook Ch. 3 boxed definition (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-045.md, p. 45): \"In the context of the health supply chain, governance is the process of establishing and implementing policies, procedures and mechanisms to ensure that the supply chain processes and the systems to manage those processes are managed effectively, ethically and in alignment with established objectives and stakeholders’ interests.\" (RA defines governance as the distribution, exercise, and accountability of decision authority across shared infrastructure; SC defines it as the process of establishing and implementing policies, procedures, and mechanisms for supply chain processes and systems.) Also related to `digital-health-governance` in Mehl et al. 2023 (glossary/full-stac.glossary.json, smart-ra#143 P8). Also framed in SFP handbook §2.3 (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-015-23-establish-governance-and-leadership.md, page-028.md, p. 16) as a structure for coordinating multiple stakeholders, defining clear roles and responsibilities, enhancing transparency, and creating a stable platform for decision-making. Both definitions are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#140, dth-sfp#1 P2).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns#glossary/full-stac/digital-health-governance"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/data-governance"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-029-341-purpose-and-framing.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/international-telecommunication-union",
