      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/traceability",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Traceability"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "traceability"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The ability to trace something. In some cases, it is interpreted as the ability to verify the history, location or application of an item by means of documented identification (14)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "SC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9, citing the WHO policy paper on traceability of medical products, ref. 14). Internal/substantive alternative in SC handbook Ch. 4 boxed definition (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-054.md, p. 54, citing GS1): \"Traceability is the ability to trace the history, application or location of an object. In a supply chain context, it is the ability to see the movement of health products across the supply chain.\" Shared across dth-sc, dth-pc, and dth-sfp; both definitions are recorded as candidates and neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#140).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-009.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/trade-item",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Trade Item"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "trade item",
        "Trade item"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Trade items are manufacturer-specific branded health products that are identifiable and unique to a particular brand or manufacturer."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "Owner decision 2026-10-31 (smart-ra#142 item 1, smart-ra#139): Trade Item is the shared WHO concept with this narrow definition from the Product Catalogue handbook Ch. 2 body (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-028.md, p. 28). The GS1 trade item is a separate external concept and the WHO term's broadMatch (every WHO Trade Item is a GS1 trade item, not the reverse: GS1's also covers services). The PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9) and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-011.md, p. 11) print the GS1 wording — \"Products or services that are priced, ordered or invoiced at any point in the supply chain\" — citing GS1 (PC ref. 13, SFP ref. 19); that sentence is recorded here as a note citing GS1, not as the WHO concept's definition.",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/generic-product"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/product-master-data"
        }
      ],
      "skos:broadMatch": [
        {
          "@id": "https://www.gs1.org/standards/id-keys/gtin"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-028.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/use-case",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Use Case"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "use case"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A use case is an example scenario of how the end-user will use the system."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11). Wording alternative in SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"An example scenario of how the end user will use a system.\" Both are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-acceptance-testing",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "User Acceptance Testing"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "UAT",
        "User acceptance testing",
        "User acceptance testing (UAT)"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "User acceptance testing (UAT) is conducted to see whether the end-users are satisfied with the end product (24)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "UAT",
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11). Wording alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) PC handbook glossary ('User acceptance testing (UAT)', who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"UAT is done to see whether the end-users are satisfied with the end product.14\" (2) SFP handbook glossary ('User acceptance testing (UAT)', who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-011.md, p. 11): \"User acceptance testing is done to see whether the end users are satisfied with the end product (20).\" All three are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-persona",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "User Persona"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "Persona",
        "persona",
        "user persona"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A generic or archetypical profile of an end-user that is representative of a single type of end-user."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording under 'User persona', verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11). Internal and cross-DTH alternatives (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) PHC handbook §3.2.1 body under 'persona' (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-012-32-conduct-end-user-research-to-understand-context.md, p. 25): \"A persona is a fictional character which represents a real group of end-users with shared characteristics, contexts, needs and challenges.\" (2) SFP handbook glossary under 'Persona' (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-010.md, p. 10): \"A generic aggregate description of a person involved in or benefiting from a health programme.\" All three are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "User Story (Requirements)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "User Story",
        "user story"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Captures a long list of features from an end-user’s perspective. It describes who the end-user is, with their feature wants or needs, and the reason for that want or need (see section 3.2.3)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11). Internal and platform alternatives (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) PHC handbook §3.2.3 body (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-012-32-conduct-end-user-research-to-understand-context.md, p. 27): \"A user story follows a standard format to write down what your end-users want from the PCPOSS: As a... [user persona], I want... [need/want], So that... [reason for need/want].\" (2) Platform glossary `user-story` (folio-assistant-core/glossary/cat-harness.glossary.json), which binds the story to a Role rather than a user persona: \"What a reader acting in a Role is trying to do, told as that role: as a <role>, I want <want>, so that <so that>.\" Also used as the functional requirements template (\"As a … / I want … / So that ...\") in SFP handbook §4.5 Table 12 (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-026-45-gather-requirements.md, page-043.md, p. 31).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/workflow",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Workflow"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "workflow"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The sequence of activities from one task to another (see section 3.3)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11). Internal and cross-DTH alternatives (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) PHC handbook §3.3 body (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-013-33-understand-the-care-pathways-and-workflows-that.md, p. 29): \"Workflows are a visual representation of the progression of activities (tasks, events, decision points) in a logical flow, illustrating the interactions within the business process (8).\" (2) SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-011.md, p. 11, citing DIIG/DAK): \"A visual representation of the progression of activities (tasks, events, decision points) in a logical flow illustrating the interactions within the business process (21).\" (PHC glossary defines a workflow as the sequence of activities itself; PHC §3.3 and SFP glossary define it as the visual representation of that progression.) All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Enabling Environment"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "enabling environment"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Attitudes, actions, policies and practices that stimulate and support effective and efficient functioning of organizations, individuals and programmes. The enabling environment includes legal, regulatory and policy frameworks and political, sociocultural, institutional and economic factors (3)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "SFP handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-009.md, p. 9, citing DIIG), matching DIIG Annex 1.1 Glossary (who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-139.md, p. 127). Shared DIIG Phase 1 concept across DTHs (smart-ra#133 S1, dth-sfp#1 §2.1 Cluster B1); recorded as a candidate.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/evaluation",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Evaluation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "evaluation"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The systematic and objective assessment of an ongoing or completed intervention with the aim of determining the fulfilment of objectives, efficiency, effectiveness, impact and sustainability (8)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "SFP handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-009.md, p. 9, citing Monitoring and evaluating digital health interventions, WHO 2016). Wording alternative in DIIG Annex 1.1 Glossary (who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-140.md, p. 128, citing WHO evaluation practice handbook, 2013): \"The systematic assessment of an ongoing or completed intervention to determine whether the intervention is fulfilling its objectives and to demonstrate an effect on health outcomes.\" Also contrasted with monitoring in SFP §6.1 (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-029-61-develop-a-monitoring-and-evaluation-plan.md, page-051.md, p. 39, quoting Pritchett et al. 2013): \"Evaluation asks whether the project is doing the right things, while monitoring asks whether the project is doing things right.\" Both definitions are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, dth-sfp#1 §2.1 Cluster B1).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/monitoring"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/health-information-system",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Health Information System"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "HIS",
        "health information system",
        "Health Information System (HIS)",
        "Health Information Systems"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A system that integrates data collection, processing, reporting, and use of the information necessary for improving health service effectiveness and efficiency through better management at all levels of health services."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "HIS",
      "skos:scopeNote": "DIIG Annex 1.1 Glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-140.md, p. 128, citing WHO 2004 Developing health management information systems; also abbreviated in DIIG page-011.md and HRH handbook who-iris/library/9789240062627-eng/sections/page-006.md). Wording alternative in PHC handbook (`dth-phc`, citing who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-001-abbreviations.md and sec-003-introduction.md): \"Health information system (HIS): socio-technical system that integrates data collection, processing, reporting, and use of health information to improve health service delivery and management across levels of the health system.\" Referenced in SFP handbook glossary under SMART Guidelines (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-011.md, p. 11) and Ch. 4 (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-021-4-determine-the-requirements.md, page-035.md, p. 23). Both definitions are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, dth-sfp#1 P2).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/health-digital-public-infrastructure"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/health-information-exchange"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-140.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/monitoring",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Monitoring"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "monitoring"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The continuous process of collecting and analysing data to compare how well an intervention is being implemented against expected results (8)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "SFP handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-010.md, p. 10, citing Monitoring and evaluating digital health interventions, WHO 2016). Wording alternative in DIIG Annex 1.1 Glossary (who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-141.md, p. 129, citing WHO evaluation practice handbook, 2013): \"The process of collecting and analysing routinely collected data to compare how well an intervention is being implemented against expected results and measure changes in performance over time.\" Both definitions are recorded as candidates; neither is chosen (smart-ra#133 S1, dth-sfp#1 §2.1 Cluster B1).",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/evaluation"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/client-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Client Registry"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "CR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Client Registry is the national authoritative source of health-specific person identity. It is the foundational health-sector component that maintains a unique, verifiable identity record for every person who accesses or is eligible to access health services within a jurisdiction."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "CR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Client Registry, 1 What It Is). Also abbreviated CR in the OpenHIE requirement identifiers (CRF-*, CRWF-*) and downstream Digital Transformation Handbooks. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-client-registry-95ffd8.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/health-facility-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Health Facility Registry"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "FR",
        "Facility Registry",
        "HFR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Health Facility Registry is the national authoritative source of identity, location, and classification data for all facilities, locations, and organisations through which health services are delivered or that are otherwise relevant to health system operations."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "FR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Health Facility Registry, 1 What It Is). Abbreviated FR in the OpenHIE Facility Registry specification references (FRF-*, FRWF-*) and FR / HFR across the Digital Transformation Handbooks. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-facility-registry-069302.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/health-workforce-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Health Workforce Registry"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "HWR",
        "Health Worker Registry"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Health Workforce Registry is the national authoritative record of identity, credential, and classification data for all health workers recognised as part of the national health workforce — including licensed or certified clinical professionals, community health workers, allied health personnel, and administrative and management staff in health-related roles."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "HWR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Health Workforce Registry, 1 What It Is). Also called Health Worker Registry (HWR) in OpenHIE alignment notes and downstream Digital Transformation Handbooks. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-workforce-registry-d1c167.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/product-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Product Registry"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "PR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Product Registry is the national authoritative source of core identity and classification data for health products — medicines, vaccines, medical devices, diagnostics, and health commodities — recognised for use within a jurisdiction."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "PR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Product Registry, 1 What It Is). Also abbreviated PR across the Digital Transformation Handbooks. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-a3e4b4.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/terminology-service",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Terminology Service"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "TS"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Terminology Service is a governed, publicly accessible service that manages, publishes, and provides access to the standardised terminologies, code systems, value sets, and concept maps used across the digital health ecosystem."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "TS",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Terminology Service, 1 What It Is). Abbreviated TS throughout the RA draft and downstream Digital Transformation Handbooks. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-terminology-service-6c5267.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/logical-information-model-repository",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Logical Information Model Repository"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "LIMR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Logical Information Model Repository is a governed, publicly accessible repository and management platform for computable clinical and administrative information models that define the logical structure, semantics, and terminology bindings of health data objects across a national digital health ecosystem."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "LIMR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Logical Information Model Repository, 1 What It Is). Abbreviated LIMR throughout the RA draft. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-73f642.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/lifelong-health-record",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Lifelong Health Record"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "LHR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Lifelong Health Record (LHR) is one or more governed data repositories, whether physically consolidated or virtually federated, that collectively maintain a longitudinal, person-centred record of an individual's key health information across care settings and over their lifetime."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "LHR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Lifelong Health Record, 1 What It Is). Abbreviated LHR throughout the RA draft. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-lifelong-health-record-7c8cd5.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/semantic-governance-infrastructure",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Semantic Governance Infrastructure"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "SGI"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Semantic Governance Infrastructure (SGI) is the cross-cutting capability that keeps the metadata registry components accurate, consistent and trustworthy, so that the semantic consistency they are intended to provide does not degrade as the health digital ecosystem grows."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "SGI",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Introduced in Section 3.4.5 and detailed in Appendix F (Table F: SGI Capability Details). A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/ch3-the-reference-architecture-for-d/p-3-4-5-474cc6.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/computable-decision-support-engine",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Computable Decision Support Engine"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "CDSE"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Computable Decision Support Engine is a governed, shared application component that delivers context-appropriate, evidence-based guidance at the point of clinical decision-making by applying computable clinical rules and knowledge artefacts to person-specific health data."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "CDSE",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Computable Decision Support Engine, 1 What It Is). Abbreviated CDSE throughout the RA draft. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-53a0a5.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/supplier-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Supplier Registry"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "SR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Supplier Registry is the authoritative master data source for identity, classification, and regulatory status of suppliers engaged in the health supply chain — including manufacturers, distributors, wholesalers, third-party logistics providers, importers, and procurement agents."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "SR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentence from Appendix C (Supplier Registry, 1 What It Is). A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-supplier-registry-c1132a.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/benefits-package-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Benefits Package Registry"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "BPR"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The Benefits Package Registry is the national authoritative record of all health benefit packages offered within a country's health financing ecosystem. It holds the definitive description of what each package covers, who is eligible in general terms, which scheme or schemes offer it, and under what rules and conditions benefits may be accessed."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BPR",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Verbatim lead sentences from Appendix C (Benefits Package Registry, 1 What It Is). Abbreviated BPR in the Appendix C comparison table. A candidate until the RA editors adopt it through the public review.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-d5d162.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/contract-and-benefits-management-system",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Contract and Benefits Management System"
        }
      ],
